# Maintenance task schedule — 5-field Vixie cron (min hour dom mon dow),
# optionally followed by an IANA timezone, then the job name. Without a
# timezone the expression is local server time; an unknown timezone name is
# rejected at startup. Trigger any job immediately with: POST /jobs/<name>.
# Override this file with --schedule <path>.

0 0 * * 0   backup          # weekly, Sunday 00:00
0 2 * * 1   rba-fx-import   # weekly, Monday 02:00
0 3 1 * *   mic-import      # monthly, 1st at 03:00 (ISO publishes monthly)
0 4 1 * *   currency-import # monthly, 1st at 04:00 (ISO 4217 + ISO 24165 / DTIF)

# Closing prices, once per market close, each entry pinned to its market's own
# timezone so a DST transition at either end can't shift the run's margin over
# the close (the Sydney<->New York offset swings 14-16h across the year). Each
# run stores, per held listing, every trading day in the last 7 whose row is
# missing or errored (days already stored ok are never re-fetched), so the
# three runs cover their own markets between them and backfill outages.
#
# The crypto run sits at 08:00 UTC, not right at the 00:00 UTC candle
# close: production job_runs history (2026-07 onward) showed the provider's
# daily crypto candle is consistently NOT yet published a few minutes or even
# a couple of hours after the UTC cut-off (a 00:30 UTC attempt failed on
# literally every run), but reliably available by the time the 07:30 UTC ASX
# run's lookback retried it. 08:00 UTC keeps a margin beyond that observed
# success point rather than relying on a same-day equity run (or, on
# weekends, a 24h-later retry) to paper over a guaranteed same-day failure.
30 17 * * 1-5   Australia/Sydney   price-import  # after the 16:00 ASX close
30 17 * * 1-5   America/New_York   price-import  # after the 16:00 NYSE close
0  8  * * *     UTC                price-import  # crypto, ~8h after the UTC cut-off

# Report snapshots, pinned to UTC (rather than local time) for the same reason
# as the crypto price-import above — an unambiguous margin past every price
# run regardless of either hemisphere's DST state. 09:00 UTC lands after all
# three price-import runs for the Sydney calendar day: the ASX close from the
# previous local afternoon, the NYSE close that landed Sydney-morning, and the
# crypto run above (~18:00-19:00 Sydney). Stores the price-dependent reports
# for every missing date in a 14-day window up to the latest date every held
# listing can be valued at with final prices. Regenerates stale or
# provisional window dates; a blocked date is skipped (reported) and retried
# on later runs.
0 9 * * *      UTC   report-snapshot
